Stage 4AO-D16 constraint-aware reduced spectrum
================================================

Scope
-----
The fixture reconstructed the baseline k=pi/4, 576x576 signed one-step
tangent map once at Nx=32, Nz=64, dx=dz=1/8, CFL=0.05, and KO sigma=0.3.
The deterministic matrix hash is 0x73c003dd70b673c6, matching committed
D14/D15 evidence.

Constraint construction
-----------------------
The signed constraint action reuses the live Hamiltonian and momentum
evaluator and the existing conformal determinant and weighted-trace helpers.
It introduces no new constraint formula. The optional encoded Z/hat-Gamma
row is omitted because no existing validated live helper supplies that
consistency relation.

The all-cell C is 160x576 with hash 0x467857d44d1b516a, epsilon-halving
discrepancy 1.635643456312e-08, rank 160, and nullity 416. Its largest and
smallest retained singular values are 3.086021845415e+03 and
4.200903287649e-01. The rank tolerance is 5.047631437490e-04 and
||CN||/||N|| is 7.476175228653e-14.

The boundary-excluded C is 130x576 with hash 0x0c67ddd102ae9f11,
epsilon-halving discrepancy 9.322136466065e-09, rank 130, and nullity 446.
Its largest and smallest retained singular values are 1.104427053408e+03
and 4.747824030723e-01. The rank tolerance is 1.029561970868e-04 and
||CN||/||N|| is 4.864109283171e-14.

Invariance and direct residuals
-------------------------------
The all-cell and interior nullspace leakage measures are respectively
7.013131751379e-02 and 5.682392577903e-02, far above the declared 1e-3
invariance gate. The all-cell projected leader has apparent
Re(Omega)=88.6510 but direct full-map residual 1.494080170318e-01. The
interior projected leader has apparent Re(Omega)=8.01662,
Im(Omega)=32.7055, and direct full-map residual 2.018919101948e-02.
Lowest-constraint representatives still have direct residuals
5.898349e-04 and 3.902230e-03, above the 1e-6 candidate gate.

The leader profiles overlap by only 0.209696. There are no qualifying
cross-projection bulk matches. The retained-evidence parser independently
recomputes the non-invariance result from emitted leakage and direct
residuals rather than trusting the fixture classification string.

Focused audit
-------------
A read-only focused audit passed the construction, SVD, leakage formula,
direct residuals, accounting, and classification. The inherited D15 layout
prints `variant=exact_gp_ghosts` in the retained matrix progress record even
though D13 preparation enforces the provisional baseline and the matrix hash
matches committed baseline evidence. This is a misleading display label, not
a numerical provenance defect.

Only the leader cross-projection overlap was retained. The corresponding
lowest-constraint overlap was not emitted. Reconstructing the matrix solely
for that non-classification-bearing number would violate D16's one-matrix
cap. The omission cannot alter the bounded classification: both nullspaces
fail the invariance gate and all four leader/lowest-constraint
representatives fail the `1e-6` direct full-map residual gate.

Efficiency
----------
The run used 576 tangent-matrix basis actions, 12 epsilon-validation tangent
actions, one random dense/direct tangent probe, and five candidate full-map
residual tangent actions: one each for the real all-cell leader and real
all-cell lowest-constraint candidate, two signed component actions for the
complex interior leader, and one for the real interior lowest-constraint
candidate. Thus `576+12+1+5=594` tangent actions produce 1,188 signed live
steps. Constraint accounting remains `576+12=588` actions and 1,176 signed
constraint evaluations. Fixture wall time was 75.6128 seconds and executable
peak RSS was 49,048 KiB.

Classification
--------------
CONSTRAINT_NULLSPACE_NOT_INVARIANT

The SVD nullspaces satisfy C N approximately zero, but the live tangent map
does not preserve either subspace. Projected eigenvalues therefore are not
interpreted as full-map modes. No GL-mode identity or critical-wavenumber
inference is made, and the Fourier scan remains suspended.
